agent	Execute Claude Code CLI	2026-10-20T08:15:34.0897363Z {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDA2zkN6Dcy2us3QEsL3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01KJLkDVmdAdUp9v3JFuoRVW","name":"mcp__safeoutputs__add_comment","input":{"body":"Thanks for the report! This is an automated first-pass triage; a maintainer will make the final call.\n\n**Reproduction:** not attempted: this is a question about intended style, and the snippets show the expected layouts rather than a bug.\n**Assessment:** This is deliberate Black style. When a call doesn't fit on one line, Black first tries to move the whole argument list onto its own indented line. If that still doesn't fit, it puts one argument per line. It never splits an argument list partway through, as in your first example. See \"How Black wraps lines\" in the style docs: https://black.readthedocs.io/en/stable/the_black_code_style/current_style.html#how-black-wraps-lines. Black has no option for this layout.\n**Next step:** If you need a specific block left as-is, you can protect it with `# fmt: off` / `# fmt: on` or `# fmt: skip`. If you want a new formatting option, a style-change request would be the right form, though Black deliberately offers few options.\n\n<sub>black-issue-triage skill v1.0.0 · suggested for maintainers: `R: not a bug`</sub>"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":555,"cache_read_input_tokens":48032,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":555,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":32,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4474dc96-a713-4f4f-b34c-3ee5ffd10fc5","uuid":"469a5ab5-445c-4bad-9b6e-f19c4e622fc8","timestamp":"2026-10-20T08:15:34.086Z","request_id":"req_011CgDA2zQ2Uby